2, 8", "gloss_language": "en"}, {"gloss": "(accord. to some also, ‘the penis’).", "gloss_language": "en"}], "synonyms": ["नदः"], "synonyms_slp1": ["nadaH"]}, {"id": "nAda", "headword": "नाद", "headword_slp1": "nAda", "fold": "nada", "headword_language": "sa", "source": "mw-cologne", "senses": [{"gloss": "नाद॑ m. (√ नद्) a loud sound, roaring, bellowing, crying, RV. &c. &c.", "gloss_language": "en"}, {"gloss": "any sound or tone, Prāt.; R. &c. (= शब्द, L.)", "gloss_language": "en"}, {"gloss": "(in the Yoga) the nasal sound represented by a semicircle and used as an abbreviation in mystical words, BhP.", "gloss_language": "en"}, {"gloss": "a praiser (= स्तोतृ), Naigh. iii, 16.", "gloss_language": "en"}], "synonyms": ["नादः"], "synonyms_slp1": ["nAdaH"]}], "nadi": [{"id": "nadI", "headword": "नदी", "headword_slp1": "nadI", "fold": "nadi", "headword_language": "sa", "source": "mw-cologne", "senses": [{"gloss": "नदी (ई), f. See नदी॑.", "gloss_language": "en"}, {"gloss": "नदी॑ f. flowing water, a river (commonly personified as a female; but See नद॑ above), RV. &c. &c. (ifc. नदिका; cf. कु-नदिका and गिरि-; ind. -नदि; cf. उप-नदि [beside -नदम्, fr. नद॑, Pāṇ. v, 4, 110])", "gloss_language": "en"}, {"gloss": "N. of 2 kinds of metre, Col.", "gloss_language": "en"}, {"gloss": "of partic. fem. stems ending in ई or ऊ (as नदी itself), Pāṇ. i, 4, 3, &c.", "gloss_language": "en"}]}, {"id": "nadi", "headword": "नदि", "headword_slp1": "nadi", "fold": "nadi", "headword_language": "sa", "source": "mw-cologne", "senses": [{"gloss": "नदि॑ m. a crier, caller, RV. v, 74, 2 (= स्तुति, Sāy.)", "gloss_language": "en"}, {"gloss": "नदि॑ mfn. ifc. See नदी.", "gloss_language": "en"}], "synonyms": ["नदिः"], "synonyms_slp1": ["nadiH"]}, {"id": "nAdi", "headword": "नादि", "headword_slp1": "nAdi", "fold": "nadi", "headword_language": "sa", "source": "mw-cologne", "senses": [{"gloss": "नादि mfn. sounding, roaring, PārGṛ.", "gloss_language": "en"}]}], "nadaDra": [{"id": "nadaDra", "headword": "नदध्र", "he